{"id": "EUVD-2026-86957", "enisaUuid": "6b49febb-64c3-31eb-b2bc-ef631131b857", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb/client: validate new EOF for zero range\n\nWhen FALLOC_FL_ZERO_RANGE is used without FALLOC_FL_KEEP_SIZE,\nsmb3_zero_range() may extend EOF without checking RLIMIT_FSIZE, allowing\nthe file to grow beyond the caller's file-size limit.\n\nFix this by calling inode_newsize_ok() before sending the zero-range\nrequest when the operation would extend EOF.\n\nReproducer, using a file on a CIFS mount:\n\n\tbash -c '\n\t        FILE=/mnt/cifs/repro\n\n\t        trap \"\" SIGXFSZ\n\t        ulimit -f 3072\n\n\t        truncate -s 2M \"$FILE\"\n\t        fallocate --zero-range -o 0 -l 4M \"$FILE\"\n\t        echo \"fallocate rc=$?\"\n\t        stat -c \"file size=%s\" \"$FILE\"\n\t'\n\nBefore this change, the operation succeeds despite the 3 MiB limit:\n\n\tfallocate rc=0\n\tfile size=4194304\n\nAfter this change, fallocate fails and leaves the file at 2 MiB.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:36:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5fbd8848f2e25c8163896ec52863df2305a3bb63", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3673f057b64abfa957e8ae84448db69369a5091a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06a4f9049cb6dc319bceec2dc813ba89add8b828", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f320ca20c273a26cd779bdb2b2e4b076a95c76f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88972e35750792e717af287dc71f42a03b5cbce4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98126", "GHSA-788x-356f-432m"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d644cb7-5d81-3b07-8d75-8aec4f7aebbf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "72c419d9b073628d3b5b0b2fc787b724f1a8c726 <88972e35750792e717af287dc71f42a03b5cbce4"}, {"id": "0fdfb2f7-fc51-3eb9-8f23-b1ced7c0cf66", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "258e22f3-28fb-3d71-950e-46e7c883e4a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "2d883076-bc57-32a2-9cb0-9563d8b253de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.1"}, {"id": "767225dd-05e5-3862-9180-61d4e8094d2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "72c419d9b073628d3b5b0b2fc787b724f1a8c726 <5fbd8848f2e25c8163896ec52863df2305a3bb63"}, {"id": "935ed92d-3282-3d4d-a9ef-495df125ab37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "72c419d9b073628d3b5b0b2fc787b724f1a8c726 <f320ca20c273a26cd779bdb2b2e4b076a95c76f6"}, {"id": "93688c46-fa1b-32ca-907e-cac57f9a0a25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "a84ccdbd-79c6-3959-815b-148a6300129c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "72c419d9b073628d3b5b0b2fc787b724f1a8c726 <06a4f9049cb6dc319bceec2dc813ba89add8b828"}, {"id": "cdb53ba0-95f4-36fd-b428-33282087b96f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "d28efa29-e559-3e64-ae68-ad6cef3f3a1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "72c419d9b073628d3b5b0b2fc787b724f1a8c726 <3673f057b64abfa957e8ae84448db69369a5091a"}, {"id": "d38f7c0b-58ed-3188-97c7-9b767fc60b01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ff32589c-b9ea-315c-9ad6-638c8e756da3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e5ed595d-c8b6-332c-9d2b-ba7b584c51f9", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}